# FlowForge environment variables
#
# EVERYTHING HERE IS OPTIONAL. FlowForge runs 100% offline with zero config:
# no key, no database, no account. Each variable below only switches one
# subsystem from its safe fallback to its live mode.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored) and uncomment only what you need.
# For Vercel, set them in Project Settings -> Environment Variables.

# =============================================================================
# 1. LINKS (shown in the product UI)
# =============================================================================
# The "Source" button and the deployment link. If NEXT_PUBLIC_REPO_URL is not
# set, the Source button points at the in-app /health conformance report
# instead, so it is never a dead link.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_REPO_URL=https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DEPLOY_URL=https://<your-deployment>.vercel.app

# =============================================================================
# 2. WEBHOOK INGRESS AUTHENTICATION  (HARDEN)
# =============================================================================
# When set, inbound webhooks MUST carry a valid HMAC-SHA256 signature over the
# raw request body:
#     x-flowforge-signature: sha256=<hex>
# Missing or invalid signature -> HTTP 401.
# When UNSET the endpoint still works (so a fresh deploy is demoable) but every
# response reports "authMode": "unsigned" and the UI surfaces that state.
# Generate a signature:
#     printf '%s' "$BODY" | openssl dgst -sha256 -hmac "$FF_WEBHOOK_SECRET" -hex
# FF_WEBHOOK_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-string

# =============================================================================
# 3. SECRETS  (HARDEN)
# =============================================================================
# Any env var named FF_SECRET_<NAME> becomes referenceable in node config as
# {{secrets.NAME}}. Values are substituted into a COPY of the node config at
# run time, so they never enter the stored workflow JSON and are redacted
# from logs. Secrets are NOT available in the browser; a node that needs one
# fails with an AUTH diagnosis rather than silently sending nothing.
# FF_SECRET_API_KEY=replace-me
# FF_SECRET_WEBHOOK_TOKEN=replace-me

# =============================================================================
# 4. DURABLE STORAGE  (HARDEN)
# =============================================================================
# The storage backend is PROBED at runtime, in this order:
#   1. remote KV (durable across redeploys and instances)  <- recommended
#   2. <project>/data on local disk (durable on a VM/container)
#   3. OS temp dir (ephemeral, per instance)
#   4. in-process memory (last resort; degrades instead of crashing)
# On Vercel serverless, local disk is ephemeral - set the KV variables below
# for durability. The active mode and the reason for it are reported at
# /api/health and shown in the product.
# KV_REST_API_URL=https://your-kv.upstash.io
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=your-token
# (or the UPSTASH_* equivalents)
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://your-kv.upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=your-token

# =============================================================================
# 5. LIVE EMAIL DELIVERY  (HARDEN)
# =============================================================================
# With no credential, the email node uses the MOCK transport: nothing is
# delivered, and the log, the node result and the run are all labelled
# SIMULATED. With a credential the SAME node, graph and code path performs a
# live send. The transport is also selectable per node in the inspector.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_your_key
# MAIL_GATEWAY_URL=https://your-gateway.example/send

# =============================================================================
# 6. AI PROVIDER  (OPTIONAL)
# =============================================================================
# If set, the "AI" node calls the OpenAI API for real completions.
# If left blank/unset, the AI node transparently falls back to a built-in,
# fully-offline mock (summarize / sentiment / keywords) so demos never break.
# The fallback is always labelled as simulated.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
